// Tier 3 — composite: a judge stacked over a stage router.
//
// The judge does not pick a target. It sets the tier the stage router falls open to,
// so a turn the signals cannot decide lands where the judge said rather than on the
// picker's default. That is the whole mechanism, and it is only visible against a
// picker that would have chosen otherwise.
//
// The retained cases matter as much: a verdict is held per identity and replayed, so a
// second turn that is not due still routes where the first one decided.
